{"seq":12,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:08:05.619Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"4760c22602096a580441e871f4443b6b6572cbc51d335bdc509dad73f3259224","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here's what I found across Moss's notes for Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL). I searched the knowledge brain, which is keyword-only here, so a semantic search could turn up more.\n\n**Ticket numbers from Moss's notes**\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025, and the patch was confirmed on 5 Oct.\n   - Source: Moss, \"Sunday prep for Ruth,\" 5 Oct 2025 (`dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday`), under \"What Changed\" and in the action items.\n\n2. **#4419**: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n   - Source: Moss, \"North cheat sheet (undated)\" (`dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet`), under \"Account & Operational Notes\" and \"What Changed.\"\n\n**Not included**\n\n- Marcus Lindqvist's \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025) also cites **#4419**, but describes it as a Gate 3 printer lag rather than scanner failures. That's Marcus's note, not Moss's, so I left it out. The two descriptions don't match, so it's worth checking which one is right before it goes in the weekly notes.\n- Moss's renewal check-in (23 Mar 2026) and pipeline digest (14 Sep 2025) mention QFL but have no ticket numbers.\n- Quarendon Freightways shows up in the same notes. It's a different company and not a Pemberline customer, so I excluded it.\n\nI can't write to your weekly notes directly, so this is for you to paste in."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
